--- Local app compatibility facts (source inspection, not live device validation) ---
README.md identifies this checkout as the IT team's Android app and cabinet screen; the Server team owns its separate API.
config/settings.json currently has "server_base_url": ""; Settings.kt reads that shipped value, so this checkout is not configured to use the new host.
Api.kt calls /auth/google, /auth/password-login, /parcels, /parcels/collect, /cabinets, and /settings, among others. These are absent from the external OpenAPI route list above. The server's pickup route is POST /transactions/verify-qr-pickup with qr_token, while this app sends POST /parcels/collect with session_code.
The external guide's health example shows mqtt=true, while the live health response above reports mqtt=false. This does not prove why the broker is unavailable.

Result: HTTPS API/docs/schema respond; authenticated app behavior was not tested without credentials. WebSocket upgrades failed, MQTT TLS on 8443 failed, MQTT WSS upgraded to neither WebSocket nor MQTT. The app contract and configured address are not ready for end-to-end use with this server.
